EPIC-EXPANSION EPIC-FIRST-BATCH

Forty-eight epic feats for level 21+. Each costs one general or eligible class
epic feat point. Use STUDY to select suboptions and review full mechanics.
Use FEATS INFO <name> or HELP <name> for individual descriptions.

Active commands: epic artisan-insight, epic efficient-trigger,
epic pierce-device, epic eidolon-ward <acid|cold|electricity|fire|sonic>.
Timers use real seconds and continue offline. No cancellation refunds.
#0

EPIC POWER KNOWLEDGE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 20, INT 21, trained Spellcraft 20, ninth-circle
psionic access.

Exact effect: Learn two additional ordinary powers from the native
psionicist catalogue at circles you can manifest. Normal discipline/list
restrictions apply. These selections do not consume normal known-power
choices and grant no PSP or epic-power unlocks.

Ranks/actions: Up to three ranks, with additional total-level gates 24 and
27. Passive. Select two different powers per rank in Study; no duplicate or
already-known choices. On respec, remove only these tagged grants; if a
power later becomes known normally it remains known.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC AUGMENTATION EFFICIENCY

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 20, INT 21, Expert Augmenting.

Exact effect: Reduce the PSP paid for an ordinary power's augmentation by 2,
never its base PSP cost. The selected augmentation must first fit both the
native manifester allowance and that power's maximum/step size. Example:
base cost 7 plus 6 legal augmentation costs 11 instead of 13, with exactly
the original +6 augmentation effect.

Limits/actions: Passive. Across this feat and any existing perk/item
discount applying to augmentation, use the largest augmentation discount,
not their sum. This feat's maximum discount is 2. No PSP refunds or bonus
augmentation points.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC FOCUS CONTINUITY

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 20, Psionic Focus, trained Concentration 20.

Exact effect: A normal successful activation of your existing psionic focus
lasts 18 rounds instead of 12. It retains all native conditions and
suppression rules.

Limits/actions: Passive upgrade to that activation. Does not refresh an
already active focus, reduce its cooldown, restore a use, stack duration
from multiple activations or alter perks that consume the focus affect.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC MENTAL BASTION

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 20, WIS 19, trained Concentration 20.

Exact effect: Gain a +4 insight bonus on native saves against charm,
domination, confusion and fear. A failed or absent save is never converted
into immunity. Does not help against unrelated death effects, energy damage
or generic Will saves.

Limits/actions: Passive. Highest applicable insight save bonus wins,
including Touch of Destiny. Stacks with Epic Will's separate feat bonus when
a Will save is actually made.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC MANIFESTING POISE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 20, Combat Manifestation, trained Concentration
20.

Exact effect: Gain +4 circumstance to Concentration checks caused by taking
damage while manifesting an ordinary power. If one hit causes multiple typed
damage packets, this bonus is applied to the native check, not repeatedly
per packet.

Limits/actions: Passive. No change to manifestation duration, actions,
interruption DC or damage. Does not help checks for spells, item activations
or other classes. Combines with Combat Manifestation; does not stack another
circumstance bonus on that same check.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC ARTISAN'S INSIGHT

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 20, INT 23, Craft Wondrous Item, trained Arcana 20.

Activation: epic artisan-insight; swift, 1/300s, out of combat. Arm for ten
rounds.

Exact effect: The next failed d20 check for a normal recipe craft or native
golem construction/repair rolls a second d20 with the same modifiers and DC,
keeping the second result. Consume the arm on that failure. Resolve the
recipe's success/failure material consumption exactly once after the reroll.

Limits: No reroll of random item quality, salvage yield, gathering, device
instability, or prerequisite validation. Does not waive recipes, skill
minimums, materials or item caps. The player must start the check while the
arm is active. Commit-time state prevents disconnect/retry rerolls.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC EFFICIENT ITEM CREATION

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 23, Craft Wondrous Item or Craft Magical Arms and
Armor, trained Arcana 23.

Exact effect: Choose one of those owned item-creation categories at Study.
Reduce eligible normal recipe completion time by 20 percentage points of the
unmodified recipe time. Add this to other time reductions, but cap their
combined reduction at 50%; final duration is rounded up to whole seconds,
minimum one second.

Ranks/actions: One rank, passive. Applies only to newly started crafts whose
recipe explicitly records the chosen category. Unclassified recipes receive
no reduction until categorized.

Limits/overlap: Efficient Crafter's existing 10% reduction participates in
the same cap. No material/gold discount, instant completion, recharge
benefit, golem construction speed bonus or change to invention/matrix
rebuilding. Cancelling retains normal penalties.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC METAMAGIC SCIENCE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 23, Metamagic Science, trained Use Magic Device 23;
three metamagic feats.

Activation: epic efficient-trigger; swift, 1/60s, arm for three rounds.

Exact effect: The next legal manually activated wand/staff spell with a
positive Metamagic Science charge surcharge pays one fewer surcharge charge.
Base activation charges are unchanged; total charge payment cannot fall
below that base. Consume on activation commitment, even if resisted or
interrupted.

Limits: No reduction in item-use DC, final spell circle, action cost or
target restrictions. Other charge discounts and this feat use the single
largest discount, not their sum. No potions, scrolls, Weird Science devices
or free activation when base charges are unavailable.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC DEVICE PENETRATION

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 20, Weird Science, Spell Penetration, Greater Spell
Penetration, trained Use Magic Device 20.

Activation: epic pierce-device; swift, 1/60s, arm for three rounds.

Exact effect: The next manual Weird Science device activation gains +4
circumstance on its first spell-resistance check. Consume the arm when the
activation commits, even if no resistance check occurs. A multi-spell device
receives the bonus on only the first check in native spell-list/target
order.

Limits/overlap: Existing Combat Calibration applies normally subject to
bonus typing; no save DC, caster level, immunity bypass or overcharge
reliability bonus. No cascade, proc, echo or automatically triggered
activation benefits.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC ANCHORED CHASSIS

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 20, Construct Stone Golem, INT 21.

Exact effect: Your active crafted golem gains +4 circumstance to defensive
checks or saves specifically against trip, knockdown, bull rush or forced
directional movement. If an effect has no defensive roll, this feat grants
no new roll or immunity.

Ranks/actions: One rank, passive. Apply once through the defensive contest,
not both a skill check and a subsequent save for the same attempt. Highest
circumstance bonus applies.

Limits/overlap: No ordinary AC, damage reduction, grappling escape, teleport
protection or player-owner bonus. Complements existing chassis HP/AC perks
without copying them. Ownership changes remove it.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC EVOLUTION RESERVE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 20, CHA 21, Eidolon class feature.

Exact effect: Gain 2 permanent evolution points per rank for the primary
eidolon's normal Study evolution budget. All native costs, rank gates, form
prerequisites and incompatibilities still apply.

Ranks/actions: Two ranks, second at total level 27. Passive; maximum +4
points. This budget explicitly adds to existing evolution-pool perks; it
does not grant another Aspect selection or another eidolon. Twin creation
uses its normal mirroring rules, not a separate editable +4 pool.

Persistence: Removing the feat requires a valid evolution respec before
finalization; do not leave an overspent creature. Recalculation grants no
current HP or resource refill.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC ADAPTIVE EIDOLON WARD

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 20, CHA 21, trained Spellcraft 20.

Activation: epic eidolon-ward <acid|cold|electricity|fire|sonic>; swift,
1/120s. Primary eidolon must be in your room.

Exact effect: The primary gains 20 flat resistance to the selected energy
for ten rounds. Selecting another energy cannot preserve the previous ward.

Stacking/counters: Use the highest applicable flat resistance against that
energy, not +20 on top of native/perk resistance. No immunity, additional
HP, natural armor or mind-affecting protection. Thus it does not reproduce
Planar Unity. Dispelling or suppression works normally;
dismissing/resummoning does not restore its spent use or duration.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC PLANAR ANCHORAGE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 20, CHA 21, trained Spellcraft 20.

Exact effect: Your primary eidolon and normal conjured creatures gain +4
circumstance on saves specifically against hostile banishment, dismissal and
effects that sever your control. If such an effect instead uses an opposed
caster-level check, add +4 to the defender's check or DC, not both.

Limits/actions: Passive; applies while the creature remains yours. No
protection against its ordinary duration expiring, your dismissal,
death/extraction or an effect that grants no save/check. No general spell
resistance, mind-affecting immunity or follower-limit exemption. Highest
circumstance bonus applies.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC FORTITUDE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: CON 21, Great Fortitude.

Exact effect: Passive +4 feat bonus to Fortitude saves. This adds to Great
Fortitude but not another copy of Epic Fortitude. Does not increase the
game's separately typed Poison or Death saves unless the actual incoming
check uses Fortitude. No action, resource, duration or repeat ranks.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC REFLEXES

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: DEX 21, Lightning Reflexes.

Exact effect: Passive +4 feat bonus to Reflex saves, adding to Lightning
Reflexes. No automatic success, evasion, damage reduction or saving throw
against an effect that normally has none. Once selectable; no
action/resource/duration.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC WILL

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: WIS 21, Iron Will.

Exact effect: Passive +4 feat bonus to Will saves, adding to Iron Will. No
mind-affecting immunity and no bonus to separately typed Death saves unless
they actually resolve as Will. Once selectable; no action/resource/duration.

Overlap: P07 can combine only for its narrow categories because its bonus is
insight, not another feat copy.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

SUPERIOR INITIATIVE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: DEX 21, Improved Initiative.

Exact effect: Increase Improved Initiative's contribution by +4, for +8
total from that feat chain. Other independently legal initiative modifiers
retain their native stacking.

Limits/actions: Passive. Does not reset existing combat timers, grant a free
opening attack, clear surprise/flat-footed state or bypass action cooldowns.
One rank.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

LEGENDARY ATHLETE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: STR 19, CON 19, trained Athletics 20, Endurance.

Exact effect: Gain +6 competence on native climbing and ordinary swimming
skill checks. For normal successful movement involving a required climb/swim
check, reduce final movement-point cost by 10, retaining the normal cost
floor.

Limits: Passive. No automatic success, new exit, wall climbing, water
breathing, flight or passage through boat-only sectors. No discount if
mounted, flying over the obstacle, teleported, or already receiving a lower
final cost from a non-stacking movement discount; apply the strongest flat
movement discount.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

IMPROVED SPELL CAPACITY

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Trained Spellcraft 20; maximum normal spell circle already
unlocked in the chosen casting class. For Summoner this is circle six, not
nine.

Exact effect: Choose one casting class at purchase. Gain one additional
maximum slot at that class's highest normal circle. Learn/prepare spells
through existing rules; this feat grants no spell knowledge, immediate
charged slot or circle above the class's normal maximum.

Ranks/actions: Two ranks, second at total level 27; both must choose the
same class. Passive. Never adds a tenth circle, grants an epic spell, or
increases PSP. Normal replenishment fills the extra capacity.

Overlap: Existing New Arcana and slot bonuses remain separate and capped by
their own rules.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

RUINOUS RAGE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Berserker 20, STR 23, Greater Rage, Power Attack.

Exact effect: While native rage is active, your own manual melee weapon
attacks ignore up to five points of the target's applicable physical damage
reduction. Effective DR cannot become negative. If several DR layers could
apply, use the native selected layer; do not subtract five from every layer.

Ranks/actions: One rank, passive. Multiple flat DR-penetration features use
the largest applicable value, not their sum.

Limits: No AC reduction, energy resistance penetration, spell or companion
benefit, immunity bypass, extra attack, or permission to destroy protected
scenery/doors. Does not change rage cost, exhaustion, duration or legality.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, STUDY, EPICFEATS
#0

EPIC-SECOND-BATCH

Sixteen further epic feats: Resistance Rebuttal, Shared Psionic Mantle; Charge-Fed
Repair, Golem Aegis, Constructbane Infusion; Resilient Bond, Spell Sharing,
Conjuration Command, Planar Triage, Evolved Summons; Trailmaster, Inspiration,
Positive Energy Bulwark, Great Smiting, Elemental Bond and Augmented Alchemy.
Use EPIC for commands and STUDY or FEATS INFO for full costs and mechanics.
Study chooses the summon doctrine and companion element before confirmation.
Cooldowns continue offline and survive respec. Great Smiting permits one rank.
#0

EPIC RESISTANCE REBUTTAL

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 20, Greater Power Penetration, trained Spellcraft
20.

Activation: epic psi-rebuttal; swift, 5 PSP, 1/60s; armed for three rounds.

Exact effect: The next ordinary power encountering positive power resistance
rolls its penetration d20 twice and keeps the better result. Apply the native
fixed penetration modifiers once. The arm is consumed at that resistance
check, including failure; it is not consumed by a power that encounters no
resistance.

Stacking: If an existing ability already gives advantage on the same check, do
not roll a third die. Does not bypass resistance automatically or change save
DC. Scope is the next target's check, not every target in an AoE.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

SHARED PSIONIC MANTLE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Psionicist 23, INT 23; know inertial armor, biofeedback or
vigor.

Activation: epic psi-mantle <ally> <power>; standard, 1/60s; pay the power's
unaugmented base PSP cost plus 8 PSP.

Exact effect: Manifest one of those three named powers on one visible grouped
ally in your room, including an owned grouped companion. This is an explicit
exception to those powers' self-only targeting. Use your current ML, no
augmentation/metamagic, duration at most ten rounds.

Limits: Does not also affect you; no copying an existing buff, spell
reflection or refund. All native stacking, dispel, suppression and temporary-
HP rules apply. It cannot duplicate a summon, heal, offensive power or epic
ward.

Shared Vigor supplies 5 finite temporary HP for at most 60 seconds, without
increasing maximum HP or healing. True temporary HP pools use the strongest
pool, never add together.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC CHARGE-FED REPAIR

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 20, Construct Stone Golem, trained Use Magic Device
20.

Activation: epic charge-repair <golem> <wand>; standard, 1/300s; consumes
three charges from a carried ordinary charged wand with a native spell of
circle 1–3. All three must be available.

Exact effect: Repair your active crafted golem for min(60, 10 + 2 × Artificer
level) HP, capped at its missing HP. May be used in combat. It is a construct
repair, with native healing suppression checks; the wand's spell is not cast.

Limits: No destroyed golem recovery, charges from devices/staves/infinite-use
items, discount from A03, spell procs, or charge refunds on overhealing.
Reject a full-HP golem before commitment. Native out-of-combat material
repairs remain available and unchanged.

Construct repair bypasses the golem penalty for healing spells and Empowered
Healing; native Blackmantle and feeding adjustments still apply.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC GOLEM AEGIS

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 23, Construct Stone Golem, INT 23.

Activation: epic golem-aegis; standard, 1/120s. Your same-room active crafted
golem must have at least 31 HP.

Exact effect: Deduct 30 HP directly from the golem and give yourself 30
temporary HP for three rounds. The golem payment cannot kill it and bypasses
damage redirection, mitigation and damage-triggered effects. The shield
follows shared temporary-HP rules.

Limits/overlap: No payment from shields, no repair to owner/golem and no
Fortress Engine transfer or Soulbound Infusion trigger from the payment.
Reject an already active Aegis shield before spending. Leaving the golem's
room or losing ownership removes the remaining shield.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC CONSTRUCTBANE INFUSION

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Artificer 25, Craft Magical Arms and Armor, trained Arcana 23.

Activation: epic constructbane <wielded weapon>; standard, 1/60s. Duration
three rounds; only one weapon per owner may carry this feat.

Exact effect: Your first successful manual weapon hit each six-second interval
against a native construct deals an additional 2d6 untyped physical damage.
The packet undergoes ordinary physical DR; this is not precision damage and
does not require a critical-vulnerable target.

Limits: Weapon must remain wielded by you. Transfer, disarm, unwield or expiry
ends the effect. No follower attacks, spell attacks, retaliation, extra item
bonus slots, salvage-value change or permanent enchantment. The six-second
proc timer belongs to the owner and cannot be reset by changing weapons.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC RESILIENT BOND

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 23, CHA 23, Life Link class feature.

Exact effect: If a damage packet would kill the primary eidolon after its
normal Life Link survival attempt has failed, allow it one DC 20 Will save. On
success reduce only that packet enough to leave it at 1 HP; on failure resolve
death normally. Consume the owner's 1/300s use before the save, either way.

Limits/actions: Passive. No protection against extraction, scripted death,
dismissal, starvation or voluntary sacrifice. No second Life Link retry,
healing, invulnerability duration or companion resurrection. Does not trigger
for the Twin Eidolon mirror.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC SPELL SHARING

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 20, trained Spellcraft 20; know one qualifying spell.

Activation: epic shared-cast <spell> [normal spell option]; normal
spellcasting action, 1/60s. Cast using a Summoner slot one circle higher than
normal; final slot must be circle six or lower.

Exact effect: Cast barkskin, blur, resist energy or stoneskin on both yourself
and the same-room primary eidolon from that one slot. Resolve each target's
stacking/immunity separately. Preserve the selected resist-energy type; use
your normal CL and ordinary spell duration. Pay all native material/resource
costs once.

Limits: Both targets must be valid before commitment. No healing, temporary-HP
grant, offensive spell, summon, epic spell, Twin mirror or third target. Does
not duplicate cast-trigger procs or restore missing HP. If interrupted,
neither buff is applied.

Native Resist Energy currently protects against all energy types and has no
selectable energy argument. Sharing retains that native behavior.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC CONJURATION COMMAND

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 20, CHA 21, Augment Summoning.

Activation: epic conjuration-command <own summon>; swift, 1/30s. One normal
conjured creature in your room; no eidolon or mirror.

Exact effect: Its next ordinary weapon/natural attack roll within two rounds
gains +4 morale to hit. If that attack hits, the primary physical damage
packet gains +8 flat damage, not multiplied on a critical. Miss or hit
consumes the order.

Limits: Grants neither an immediate attack nor an action reset. Does not
affect spell attacks, each claw separately, AoE, extra damage packets or
subsequent attacks. Highest morale attack bonus applies. Existing Beast
Commander and stat bonuses retain their own rules; this is a short, one-attack
command.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC PLANAR TRIAGE

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 20, sixth-circle Summoner access, CHA 21.

Activation: epic planar-triage; standard, expend one available sixth-circle
Summoner slot, 1/300s. Primary eidolon must be alive, injured and in your
room.

Exact effect: Heal the primary for min(100, floor(0.20 × its max HP)), minimum
1 before the normal healing pipeline. It receives no stat change or temporary
HP. Native healing penalties may reduce the result.

Limits: No use on a mirror, purchased pet, other player's eidolon or
dismissed/dead creature. No resurrection, lost-slot refund, cooldown reset or
extra heal from Life Bond. If native healing suppression rejects all healing
before commitment, reject the command without spending a slot.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC EVOLVED SUMMONS

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Summoner 23, Improved Augment Summoning, trained Spellcraft 23.

Exact effect: Choose one doctrine at Study: Aquatic or Watchful. Newly created
normal conjured creatures receive that doctrine for their original remaining
summon lifetime. Aquatic grants native natural-swimmer status and underwater
breathing; Watchful grants +4 competence Perception and native scent
detection.

Limits/actions: Passive. No extra attacks, spellcasting, bonus follower slot,
additional summon, increased duration or swimming through boat-only exits. Do
not grant a second copy of an ability already possessed. Existing stronger
competence Perception wins. Choose once, changed only through a normal feat
respec.

Persistence: Store provenance and original summon expiry, so pet restore can
reapply the doctrine without creating fresh lifetime or benefits for purchased
pets. This uses a restricted doctrine rather than an unrestricted evolution
editor on every summoned mob.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC TRAILMASTER

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: WIS 21, Track, trained Nature 23, trained Perception 20.

Exact effect: Gain +6 competence to the native tracking check. While following
an already recorded trail through a water or flying sector, ignore up to 10
points of its terrain-related tracking penalty. Do not remove age, concealment
or magical anti-tracking penalties.

Limits: Passive. Does not fabricate a trail, reveal a hidden room/exit, report
a remote player's live location or track through teleportation. Where the
engine records no trail at all, it provides only the skill bonus. Existing
trail visibility, age limits and builder restrictions remain.

Native tracking currently has no recorded room trails or separate terrain
penalty. Only the +6 competence tracking bonus applies; range and existing
target lookup are unchanged.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC INSPIRATION

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Bard 20, CHA 23, Bardic Music; trained Perform 20.

Exact effect: Increase Dance of Protection’s AC and Will-save contributions
and Song of Heroism’s attack-roll and damage-roll contributions by +1 per
rank. Modify each original contribution, retaining its native inherent type,
targeting and duration. These four numeric components are the complete
whitelist.

Ranks/actions: Two ranks, second requires total level 27 and Bard 23. Passive;
at most +2 to an eligible contribution. Duplicate singers still use normal
highest-bonus rules.

MUD boundary: The tabletop morale/competence/dodge wording is replaced
deliberately because these native songs use inherent bonuses. No extra hit
dice, ability scores, DR, haste, healing, spell damage, duration, skill
success chance or hostile-song DC. Song of Heroism’s existing haste bit is
unchanged.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

POSITIVE ENERGY BULWARK

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Cleric 20 or Paladin 20, CHA 21, Channel Energy, native
permission to channel positive energy.

Activation: epic positive-bulwark; standard, 1/300s, plus one available native
Channel Energy use. Three-round duration.

Exact effect: At commitment and six and twelve seconds later, deal 2d6
positive-energy damage to each legal hostile undead in your room, using the
native channel-undead damage path. Each pulse allows Will half, DC 10 +
floor(qualifying class level / 2) + CHAmod. Snapshot the qualifying class and
modifier at activation; if both classes qualify choose the higher class level,
not their sum.

Limits: No living targets, healing pulses, automatic turning/destruction,
negative levels or channel-use refunds. Recheck PvP, room and target legality
each pulse. Aura ends on death, unconsciousness or extraction, cannot overlap
itself, and generates no secondary channel procs. Do not inherit damage
increases from unrelated active Channel Energy uses.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

GREAT SMITING

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Paladin 20 or Blackguard 20, CHA 23, the corresponding Smite
Evil/Smite Good feature.

Activation: epic great-smite; swift, 1/300s, arm for three rounds. The next
native manual smite attack consumes its ordinary smite use and normal action
as well as this already committed arm.

Exact effect: If that attack hits a target eligible for the chosen native
smite, deal +L physical damage, where L is the class level supplying that
smite. Apply as a separate packet subject to normal physical defenses, never
critical multiplication.

Ranks/limits: One rank. Miss, expiry, wrong-alignment target after commitment
or loss of the smite arm gives no refund. No extra smite use, immunity bypass,
alignment conversion or bonus on every later attack against a marked target.
Audit existing callers of this ID before enabling it so its old per-rank
damage cannot also apply.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

LEGENDARY COMPANION: ELEMENTAL BOND

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Druid 20 or Ranger 20, Animal Companion, WIS 21, trained
Nature/Survival 20.

Exact effect: Permanently choose acid, cold, electricity or fire at Study.
Your single active native animal companion's first successful normal melee
attack each six-second interval deals an additional 1d6 of that energy.
Snapshot the type from the owner's feat, not a rerolled summon template.

Ranks/actions: One rank, passive. Owner-level six-second timer persists across
pet dismissal, replacement and restoration. No extra attack, follower slot,
new companion type or rider on spell/proc/retaliation attacks.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
#0

EPIC AUGMENTED ALCHEMY

Character level 21+. Cost: one general or eligible class epic feat point.

Prerequisites: Alchemist 20, INT 23, native bomb feature; trained Craft
(Alchemy) 20.

Activation: epic augment-bomb <prepared bomb slot> <sacrificial bomb slot>;
swift, 1/60s. Both slots must contain prepared normal fire bombs and be
distinct. Consume the sacrificial bomb immediately and bind the other slot for
three rounds.

Exact effect: Your next manual throw of the bound bomb uses its normal action,
attack and consumption rules. On a successful direct hit, add 4d6 fire damage
to the primary target only. Use the bomb's normal direct-hit save outcome, if
any, for the extra packet. A miss still consumes the bomb and feat use.

Limits/overlap: Splash, sticky ticks, chain reactions and secondary targets
gain nothing. Expiry discards the bonus, not the bound bomb; the sacrificed
bomb is never restored. Discarding/changing the bound slot cancels the arm.
Existing bomb perks apply to the original attack, not a second proc chain. No
bonus to healing/control bombs, extra prepared slots or exception to native
bomb-making recovery. Slot identity and prepaid sacrifice require atomic saved
state.

See also: EPIC-EXPANSION, EPIC-SECOND-BATCH, STUDY
